<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 27 April, from 1521 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/philippines" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippines.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1521 CE <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ferdinand Magellan is killed on Mactan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Magellan died fighting the forces of the chief Lapulapu in the Philippines. Under Juan Sebastián Elcano, one ship of his fleet returned to Spain in 1522, completing the first circumnavigation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1650 CE <span class="tih-ago">376 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Montrose's royalists are routed at Carbisdale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Marquess of Montrose, landing in Scotland for the exiled Charles II, was defeated by Covenanter forces. He was captured and hanged in Edinburgh a month later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1791 CE <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Morse is born in Massachusetts</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Morse, painter turned inventor, was born in Charlestown. He developed an electric telegraph and, with Alfred Vail, the code that bears his name.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1810 CE <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Beethoven dates the manuscript of Für Elise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Beethoven's autograph of the Bagatelle in A minor carried the date 27 April 1810. Unpublished in his lifetime, it appeared in 1867 and became one of the best-known piano pieces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Partisans capture Mussolini at Dongo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Disguised in a German greatcoat in a convoy heading north, Benito Mussolini was recognised and seized by Italian partisans near Lake Como. He was shot the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1994 CE <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">South Africa holds its first all-race elections</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Millions of Black South Africans voted for the first time. The ANC won decisively and Nelson Mandela became president, ending the apartheid order. The date is now Freedom Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
